stdout | Tree-sitter parse all files in a project for specified rebar.config file
stdout |
stdout | Usage: elp parse-elp [OPTIONS]
stdout |
stdout | Options:
stdout |       --project <PROJECT>    Path to directory with project, or to a JSON file [default: .]
stdout |       --module <MODULE>      Parse a single module from the project, not the entire project
stdout |       --file <FILE>          Parse a single file from the project, not the entire project. \nThis
stdout |                              can be an include file or escript, etc
stdout |       --to <TO>              Path to a directory where to dump result files
stdout |       --no-diags             Do not print the full diagnostics for a file, just the count
stdout |       --experimental         Report experimental diagnostics too, if diagnostics are enabled
stdout |       --as <PROFILE>         Rebar3 profile to pickup [default: test]
stdout |       --dump-includes        Report the resolution of include directives for comparison with OTP
stdout |                              ones
stdout |       --rebar                Run with rebar
stdout |       --include-generated    Also process generated modules
stdout |       --serial               Parse the files serially, not in parallel
stdout |       --use-cli-severity     If specified, use the provided CLI severity mapping instead of the
stdout |                              default one
stdout |       --format <FORMAT>      Customize the output format (defaults to human-readable) [possible
stdout |                              values: json]
stdout |       --report-system-stats  Report system memory usage and other statistics
stdout |       --severity <SEVERITY>  Minimum severity level to report [possible values: error, warning,
stdout |                              weak_warning, information]
stdout |   -h, --help                 Print help
stdout |
stdout | Global options:
stdout |       --log-file <LOG_FILE>  
stdout |       --erl <ERL>            
stdout |       --escript <ESCRIPT>    
stdout |       --no-log-buffering     
stdout |       --no-buck-generated    Deprecated (no-op): buck project loading always builds generated code
stdout |       --buck-quick-start     Deprecated (no-op): buck project loading always builds generated code
stdout |       --color <WHEN>         Use color in output [default: always] [possible values: always, never,
stdout |                              auto]
